  "interpretation": "In this refined-interior portrait context, director micro-story framing improved the primary visual_event_coherence score by 1.50 over a semantically matched static description. Aesthetic quality improved by 0.75 and the overall mean improved by 0.50, while semantic compliance was unchanged and technical-defect cleanliness decreased by 0.25. The micro-story group also showed lower across-replicate variability. This single small-N run supports the tested hypothesis in this context, but it does not establish universal superiority. Replication across actions, environments, subjects, props, and routes is required before broader generalization.",
